# Force LF in the repository regardless of the checkout platform's line
# ending settings. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# normalizes to CRLF locally while CI (Linux) checks out LF — Biome (and any
# other tool that's line-ending sensitive) then disagrees with itself between
# a local run and CI. Git still stores LF blobs either way; this just stops
# local autocrlf from producing CRLF files that look "changed" against CI.
* text=auto eol=lf
